+"""Panel round 10, task A2: the identity tier that survives a checkout with NO `.git`.
+
+THE DEFECT THESE CONTROLS GUARD. The A2 repair rebases an archived falsifier's
+stale absolute path onto the overlay, and it recognises the path only if it can
+tell that the path names a checkout of THIS project. Identity came from the git
+remote, with the folder name as the only fallback. A `git clone` carries a
+remote; NOTHING ELSE DOES. Measured 2026-09-10 in the panel sandbox -- `git`
+2.50.1 on PATH, no `.git` directory -- identity collapsed to the folder name
+`repo`, the rebase recognised 0 of the 35 stale paths, and the suite this file
+sits beside went RED:
+
+    2 failed, 18 passed, 1 skipped
+      TestTheReplayRebaseIsBounded::test_it_rebases_this_project_named_from_another_checkout
+      TestTheRejectionClassifier::test_the_real_rejection_count_is_location_independent
+
+`bench/panel_sandbox.py:43` sets `_NEVER_COPY = frozenset({".git"})`, so the
+degraded state is every panel run this project performs -- and every reader who
+takes the GitHub "Download ZIP", the Zenodo archive this project publishes, a
+`git archive` tarball, or a vendored copy. The task is "make the suite pass in a
+fresh clone"; a reader who does not use `git clone` saw a suite made red BY the
+fix for that task.
+
+WHY THESE CONTROLS BIND, stated because this project has caught 8 of its own
+mutation tests passing against the broken state, and 2 of the maintainer's on
+this very task. Every control that must detect the tier's absence asserts on the
+identity SOURCE, never merely on the presence of the name `Constraint_Engineering`
+in the name set. In the maintainer's own checkout the folder IS named
+`Constraint_Engineering`, so a name-membership assertion passes with the whole
+tier deleted -- which is the exact trap that made the maintainer's first identity
+control vacuous. Mutation-verified both ways; see the commentary on each class.
+
+THE NO-GIT CONDITION IS SIMULATED BY SUPPRESSING THE REMOTE LOOKUP, not by
+deleting a `.git` directory. That is the stronger construction: it reproduces the
+degraded state in ANY checkout, including the maintainer's, so these controls
+cannot pass merely because the machine they run on happens to carry a remote.
